{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"EPIC 2ddd WAVE DISPATCH. Board: 1 closed (6f18), 4 in_progress (111a+4329 merged-but-unclosed, 1cf6 + 73b8 + 7931 in flight), 17 open.\nLeaf 7931 (Gerrit 2064): the blocking LLM-Review -1 said the consolidated _ticket_id had no behavioural test of its contract. Added two tests - resolution order (explicit ticket_id input beats target_ticket, empty falls back, non-str coerced) and the refusal path (ValueError naming the step and both ways to supply a ticket). Proved teeth by mutation: reversing the 'or' operands killed the order test; dropping step_id from the message killed the refusal test. lint + mypy (626 files) clean. Amended, re-pushed; the -1 was cleared as outdated. Votes pending.\nCLOSE BLOCKERS DIAGNOSED (they are DIFFERENT, not one bug): 4329 fails with stale-material - its description grew 4392->8980 chars because implementation findings were appended to the DESCRIPTION rather than to comments, and 8980 is OVER the 8000-char plan-review admission cap, so a naive re-review would BLOCK unread. Condensed to 6412 chars preserving all substance. 111a fails on unticked AC checkboxes (ticking is attestation-safe; box state is normalised out of the material fingerprint) - each box must be verified against the merged code before ticking. A close-out agent owns both.\nDispatched 13 end-to-end leaf agents against a shared brief (tmp/LEAF_BRIEF.md): 1dd5 and dff2 (already certified, straight to claim), fcb7 (stale-code, needs re-review), d6e3, 25b4, 7e0d, 4cee, d075, 2e0f, 4144, 44ff, 7f54, a4d7. Each is told the specific known defect in its plan where one was found, and that EVERY plan checked so far has been materially wrong about the code.\nBlocked dependents and their prerequisites: 3436 <- 6f18(closed)+1cf6; da84 <- d6e3; 77e7 <- a4d7. Dispatch these as their prerequisites close."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787376281505388001,"uuid":"0a2b9d77-a4a4-4e6f-9d76-c55085b57461"}